## When to use

When the user asks about the contents of an image file: reading a screenshot, finding an error message in a UI, comparing two images, describing a diagram or photo. Use it whenever your own model cannot see images.

## Command

Run the script from the user's working directory, using the absolute path to this Skill:

```bash
node <this Skill's directory>/scripts/run.mjs describe --image <path> [--image <path> ...] [--prompt "<question>"] [--max-tokens <n>]
```

- `--image`: a local PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF file, at most 20 MB. Repeat for up to 8 images.
- `--prompt`: what to ask about the images. Put the user's actual question here. Default: "Describe this image."
- `--max-tokens`: the longest answer to allow. Default 1024.
- `--timeout`: seconds to wait. Default 120.

The answer is printed to stdout as plain text.
